Aim: Inspect browser artifacts, history, cookies and saved data.

Theory:

1)Browser Artifacts:
       Digital traces including history (Urls + timestamps), cookies (tracking tokens), local storage (HTML5 data) and saved Credentials

2) Storage Location:
       Firefox (~/ mozilla/Firefox/)

3)Privacy Risks:
       ↳ Third party track users accross websites without consent
          Missing (Http Only) flag enables session hijacking by Xss.
       ↳ Saved Passwords decryptables by local malware.
          local storage persists idefinitely Containing JWT tokens and PII.

4) Key Cookie Attributes:
        (Secure) (HTTPS only), (HTTP only) (ne JS access), (Demain) Cindicates tracking scope).

Methodology:

1)Setup
      ↳ sudo apt update des mkdir ~/browser-forensics 
       cd ~/browser-forensics.

2)Manual Inspection:
       Open Firefox F-12 Storage tab View cookies/Local storage →Ctrl+H (for history).

3) Hack Browser Data:
      ↳ Download, extmet, run [./hack-browser-Dota-ball-b jsendir resure]

4)Fox Hunter:
     git clone pip install-s requirements txt- ron with (-A) flag for analysis

5)Risk Analysis:
     grep for tracking domains (doubleclick/analytics) and check (httpOnly) blogs.

Future Scope:

Develop a real-time browser privacy scoring extensions. that detects tracking cookies and exposed session tokens                                                                        
